Below is a complete, copy-and-paste-ready recipe for “on-the-fly” icons in **MapLibre GL JS**.  
It works the same way the original Mapbox GL JS `styleimagemissing` event does: when the style asks for an image that isn’t in the sprite, you intercept the request, load the image yourself (from a URL, a data-URI, a canvas, etc.), add it to the map’s image cache, and the layer instantly picks it up.

---

## TL;DR

```js
// 1️⃣ Wait for the map to be ready
map.on('load', () => {
  // 2️⃣ Listen for missing-image events
  map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
    const id = e.id;                     // the name the style tried to use
    const url = `/icons/${id}.png`;      // ← decide where to fetch it from

    try {
      // 3️⃣ Load the image (any of the three helpers works)
      const img = await loadImage(url); // returns an HTMLImageElement or ImageBitmap

      // 4️⃣ Add it to the map’s internal image cache
      map.addImage(id, img, { sdf: false, pixelRatio: 2 });

      // 5️⃣ (optional) force a repaint if the layer is already on the map
      map.triggerRepaint();
    } catch (err) {
      console.warn(`⚠️ Could not load icon "${id}" from ${url}`, err);
    }
  });
});

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Helper that works in every modern browser (fetch → createImageBitmap) */
async function loadImage(url) {
  const resp = await fetch(url, { mode: 'cors' });
  if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${resp.status}`);
  const blob = await resp.blob();
  // createImageBitmap is faster & works off-screen, but falls back to Image if unavailable
  return (self.createImageBitmap ? await createImageBitmap(blob) : await imgFromBlob(blob));
}

/* Fallback that creates a regular HTMLImageElement */
function imgFromBlob(blob) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const img = new Image();
    img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';
    img.onload = () => resolve(img);
    img.onerror = reject;
    img.src = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  });
}
```

That’s it. Every time the style references an icon that isn’t already in the sprite, the `styleimagemissing` handler runs, fetches the PNG (or SVG, or even a canvas-generated image), registers it with `map.addImage()`, and the layer instantly shows the new icon.

---

## Why This Works (and why you can’t just “edit the sprite”)

* **Sprites are static** – they are a single PNG + JSON file that the style loads once at startup. Changing them after the style has been parsed would require a full `setStyle()` call, which would destroy all your runtime state.
* **`map.addImage()` is the public API for dynamic images** – it stores the image in an internal cache that the renderer consults *every* time it draws a symbol layer. The cache lives alongside the sprite, so you can mix static-sprite icons and runtime-added icons without any conflict.
* **`styleimagemissing` is a built-in “fallback” hook** – MapLibre GL JS fires this event *exactly* when a layer’s `icon-image` property resolves to a name that isn’t in the cache. It gives you a perfect place to plug in your own loader.

---

## Step-by-Step Walk-through

### 1️⃣ Wait for the map to be ready

You must attach the listener **after** the `load` event (or any later point) because the `styleimagemissing` event is only emitted once the style has been parsed.

```js
map.on('load', () => {
  // … attach listener here …
});
```

### 2️⃣ Listen for `styleimagemissing`

```js
map.on('styleimagemissing', (e) => {
  // e.id is the string the style tried to use, e.sourceId is undefined for sprites
});
```

*The event object only contains `{ id: string }` – you decide where to get the image from.*

### 3️⃣ Load the image

You have three common ways to get an image into a form that `addImage` accepts:

| Method | Returns | When to use |
|--------|---------|-------------|
| `map.loadImage(url, callback)` | `HTMLImageElement` (or `ImageBitmap` on newer browsers) | Quick one-liner, but callback-based. |
| `fetch → createImageBitmap` (as in the helper above) | `ImageBitmap` | Faster, works off-screen, works with CORS-enabled resources. |
| Draw on a `<canvas>` and call `canvas.transferToImageBitmap()` | `ImageBitmap` | When you need to generate the icon programmatically (e.g., text, charts). |

All three are accepted by `map.addImage()`.

### 4️⃣ Register the image

```js
map.addImage(id, img, {
  // Optional flags:
  sdf: false,          // true if the image is an SDF (signed distance field) for tinting
  pixelRatio: 2,       // match the @2x version if you have one
  stretchX: [],        // for sprite-sheet slicing – not needed for single icons
  stretchY: []
});
```

If you try to add an image with a name that already exists, `addImage` throws. You can guard against that with `if (!map.hasImage(id)) …`.

### 5️⃣ Force a repaint (usually not needed)

If the layer that requested the missing icon is already on the map, the renderer will automatically pick up the newly added image on the next frame. In rare cases (e.g., you added the image after the layer’s `icon-image` property was already evaluated) you can call:

```js
map.triggerRepaint();
```

---

## Full Example – A Real-World Use-Case

Suppose you have a GeoJSON source of points, each feature has a property `icon` that matches a file name in `/icons/`. Some icons are shipped in the static sprite, others are only available on demand.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Dynamic Icons with MapLibre GL JS</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>#map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        points: {
          type: 'geojson',
          data: {
            type: 'FeatureCollection',
            features: [
              { type: 'Feature', geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.4, 37.8] }, properties: { icon: 'restaurant' } },
              { type: 'Feature', geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.41, 37.81] }, properties: { icon: 'cafe' } },
              { type: 'Feature', geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.79] }, properties: { icon: 'custom-01' } } // not in sprite
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      layers: [
        {
          id: 'points',
          type: 'symbol',
          source: 'points',
          layout: {
            // The icon name comes directly from the feature property
            'icon-image': ['get', 'icon'],
            'icon-size': 1,
            'icon-allow-overlap': true
          }
        }
      ],
      // Optional: a minimal sprite that contains only a few fallback icons
      sprite: 'https://example.com/sprite/sprite.json'
    },
    center: [-122.4, 37.8],
    zoom: 13
  });

  // ---- Dynamic-icon handler -------------------------------------------------
  map.on('load', () => {
    map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
      const id = e.id;                     // e.g. "custom-01"
      const url = `/icons/${id}.png`;      // adjust to your own folder/extension

      // Bail out early if we already added it (race condition safety)
      if (map.hasImage(id)) return;

      try {
        const img = await loadImage(url);
        map.addImage(id, img, { sdf: false, pixelRatio: 2 });
        // No need to call triggerRepaint – the layer will re-evaluate automatically
      } catch (err) {
        console.warn(`⚠️ Could not load dynamic icon "${id}" from ${url}`, err);
        // Optionally add a fallback placeholder:
        if (!map.hasImage('missing-icon')) {
          const placeholder = await loadImage('/icons/missing.png');
          map.addImage('missing-icon', placeholder);
        }
        // Force the layer to use the placeholder
        map.setLayoutProperty('points', 'icon-image', ['coalesce', ['get', 'icon'], 'missing-icon']);
      }
    });
  });

  // ---- Helper: fetch → ImageBitmap -----------------------------------------
  async function loadImage(url) {
    const resp = await fetch(url, { mode: 'cors' });
    if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${resp.status}`);
    const blob = await resp.blob();
    return (self.createImageBitmap ? await createImageBitmap(blob) : await imgFromBlob(blob));
  }

  function imgFromBlob(blob) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      const img = new Image();
      img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';
      img.onload = () => resolve(img);
      img.onerror = reject;
      img.src = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    });
  }
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**What this does**

1. The style contains a *tiny* sprite (maybe just a generic “missing” icon).  
2. The `points` layer asks for `icon-image` = the value of each feature’s `icon` property.  
3. For `restaurant` and `cafe` the sprite already has those names → they render instantly.  
4. For `custom-01` the sprite has no entry → `styleimagemissing` fires.  
5. The handler fetches `/icons/custom-01.png`, registers it, and the point instantly shows the new picture.  
6. If the fetch fails, we fall back to a built-in `missing-icon` placeholder.

---

