Below is a complete, step-by-step recipe for “on-the-fly” icons in **MapLibre GL JS** when the style’s sprite does not contain the requested image.  
The core idea is to listen for the `styleimagemissing` event, fetch or generate the image yourself, and register it with `map.addImage()`. Once the image is added, any layer that references the same `icon-image` name will instantly start drawing the new icon – no page reload or style rebuild required.

---

## 1️⃣ Why the error happens

When a layer’s `layout.icon-image` (or `layout.text-field` with an `icon-` token) refers to a name that is **not** present in the style’s sprite, MapLibre throws a `StyleImageMissingError` and the layer is rendered with a transparent placeholder.  
The library deliberately does **not** silently ignore the missing image because it wants you to know that the style is incomplete.

> **Key point:** The error is emitted as a **`styleimagemissing`** event, which gives you a perfect hook to supply the missing asset yourself.

---

## 2️⃣ The “official” way – `styleimagemissing` event

```js
// Assume `map` is an already-created MapLibre GL JS instance
map.on('load', () => {
  // 1️⃣ Register a global handler for any missing image
  map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
    const missingId = e.id;               // the name the style tried to use
    console.warn(`Missing icon "${missingId}" – loading it now…`);

    try {
      // 2️⃣ Load the image (you can fetch from a URL, a data-uri, a canvas, etc.)
      const image = await loadIcon(missingId); // <-- see helper below

      // 3️⃣ Register it with the map
      //    `sdf: true` if you are using signed-distance-field icons (e.g. Mapbox icons)
      map.addImage(missingId, image, { sdf: false, pixelRatio: window.devicePixelRatio });

      // 4️⃣ (Optional) Force a repaint if the layer was already drawn once
      map.triggerRepaint();
    } catch (err) {
      console.error(`Failed to load icon "${missingId}":`, err);
    }
  });
});
```

### What the handler receives

| Property | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| `e.id`   | The **icon name** the style tried to look up (exactly the string you would put in `layout.icon-image`). |
| `e.source` | The source of the request – always `"style"` for sprite look-ups. |
| `e.type` | Always `"styleimagemissing"` (useful if you attach the same listener to multiple maps). |

---

## 3️⃣ Helper: `loadIcon(id)` – fetch or generate the image

You can implement `loadIcon` in any way that makes sense for your app:

| Source | Example implementation |
|--------|------------------------|
| **Remote PNG/JPEG** | `map.loadImage(url)` (built-in convenience) |
| **Data-URI** | `await fetch(dataUri).then(r => r.blob()).then(createImageBitmap)` |
| **Canvas / SVG** | Draw on a `<canvas>` or convert an `<svg>` to a bitmap |
| **Font-awesome / Icon fonts** | Render a glyph onto a canvas, then `createImageBitmap` |
| **Dynamic generation** | Use a library like `sharp` (Node) or `fabric.js` (browser) to draw on-the-fly |

Below are three common patterns.

#### 3.1 Remote PNG via `map.loadImage`

```js
async function loadIcon(id) {
  // Convention: your icon files live under /icons/<id>.png
  const url = `/icons/${encodeURIComponent(id)}.png`;
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    map.loadImage(url, (error, image) => {
      if (error) return reject(error);
      resolve(image);
    });
  });
}
```

#### 3.2 Data-URI (e.g., base64-encoded SVG)

```js
async function loadIcon(id) {
  // Suppose you have a map of id → data-uri somewhere
  const dataUri = ICON_DATA_URIS[id];
  if (!dataUri) throw new Error(`No data-uri for ${id}`);

  const response = await fetch(dataUri);
  const blob = await response.blob();
  return await createImageBitmap(blob);
}
```

#### 3.3 Canvas-generated icon (e.g., a colored circle)

```js
async function loadIcon(id) {
  // Example: id = "circle-red-24"
  const [shape, color, sizeStr] = id.split('-');
  const size = Number(sizeStr); // e.g., 24

  const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
  canvas.width = canvas.height = size;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

  if (shape === 'circle') {
    ctx.fillStyle = color;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(size / 2, size / 2, size / 2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
  }
  // … add more shapes as you like

  return await createImageBitmap(canvas);
}
```

> **Tip:** `createImageBitmap` is fast and returns an `ImageBitmap` that `addImage` accepts directly. If you prefer the older `HTMLImageElement`, you can also pass that, but `ImageBitmap` avoids an extra layout pass.

---

## 4️⃣ Using the newly added image in a layer

If the layer already exists and references the missing name, you **don’t** need to touch the layer definition – once `addImage` finishes, MapLibre will automatically re-render the layer with the new icon.

If you are adding a brand-new layer after the image is loaded, just reference the same `icon-image` name:

```js
map.addLayer({
  id: 'dynamic-points',
  type: 'symbol',
  source: 'my-points',
  layout: {
    'icon-image': 'my-custom-icon', // <-- must match the id you added
    'icon-size': 1.2,
    'icon-allow-overlap': true
  }
});
```

---

## 5️⃣ Advanced options for `addImage`

| Option | Description | Typical use |
|--------|-------------|-------------|
| `sdf` | **Signed-distance-field** – set to `true` if the image is an SDF (e.g., Mapbox’s default icons). Allows you to recolor the icon with `icon-color`. | Font-awesome-style icons, Mapbox-Maki icons |
| `pixelRatio` | Device pixel ratio for retina displays. Usually `window.devicePixelRatio`. | Improves sharpness on high-DPI screens |
| `stretchX` / `stretchY` | Define stretchable regions for 9-slice scaling (rarely needed for simple icons). | UI-style markers that need to stretch |
| `content` | An array `[left, top, right, bottom]` that defines the *icon’s* anchor box relative to the image dimensions. | When you need a custom anchor point (e.g., bottom-center) |

Example with an SDF icon:

```js
map.addImage('my-sdf-icon', imageBitmap, { sdf: true, pixelRatio: 2 });
```

Now you can recolor it on the fly:

```js
map.setPaintProperty('my-layer', 'icon-color', '#ff6600');
```

---

## 6️⃣ Caching – avoid re-fetching the same icon

If you expect the same missing icon to appear many times (e.g., many features reference `"restaurant"`), keep a **Set** or **Map** of already-loaded ids:

```js
const loadedIcons = new Set();

map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
  const id = e.id;
  if (loadedIcons.has(id)) return; // already added earlier

  try {
    const img = await loadIcon(id);
    map.addImage(id, img);
    loadedIcons.add(id);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
  }
});
```

---

## 7️⃣ Full-working example (copy-paste)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – Dynamic Icons</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json', // any style without the custom icons
    center: [-122.447303, 37.753574],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // Dummy GeoJSON source with a feature that references a non-existent icon
  const geojson = {
    type: 'FeatureCollection',
    features: [{
      type: 'Feature',
      geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.447303, 37.753574] },
      properties: { name: 'Dynamic Icon' }
    }]
  };

  map.on('load', () => {
    // Add source + layer that uses a missing icon name
    map.addSource('points', { type: 'geojson', data: geojson });
    map.addLayer({
      id: 'points',
      type: 'symbol',
      source: 'points',
      layout: {
        'icon-image': 'my-dynamic-pin', // <-- not in the sprite
        'icon-size': 1,
        'text-field': ['get', 'name'],
        'text-offset': [0, 1.5],
        'text-anchor': 'top'
      }
    });

    // ---------- Dynamic-icon handler ----------
    const loaded = new Set();

    map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
      const id = e.id;
      if (loaded.has(id)) return; // already done

      console.log(`🔎 Need icon "${id}" – loading…`);

      try {
        // Example: fetch a PNG from /icons/<id>.png
        const url = `/icons/${encodeURIComponent(id)}.png`;
        const img = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
          map.loadImage(url, (err, image) => err ? reject(err) : resolve(image));
        });

        map.addImage(id, img, { pixelRatio: window.devicePixelRatio });
        loaded.add(id);
        console.log(`✅ Icon "${id}" added`);
      } catch (err) {
        console.error(`❌ Could not load "${id}"`, err);
      }
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

*Replace `/icons/<id>.png` with the real path to your icon assets, or swap the `loadIcon` implementation for any of the helpers shown earlier.*

---

## 8️⃣ Common pitfalls & how to avoid them

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **`Error: Image "foo" not found in style sprite` keeps repeating** | The `styleimagemissing` handler never resolves (e.g., you forgot to call `resolve`/
